{"name":"Coventry Blue","hex":"#8ba9bc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Coventry blue","blocks":[{"text":"Coventry blue was a blue cloth woven and dyed with woad in Coventry. The permanence of the colour led to the phrase \"as true as Coventry blue\" or \"true blue\"."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coventry_blue"},{"title":"Coventry","blocks":[{"text":"Coventry is a cathedral city and metropolitan borough in the West Midlands county, in England, on the River Sherbourne. Coventry had been a large settlement for centuries. Founded in the early Middle Ages, its city status was formally recognised in a charter of 1345. The city is governed by Coventry City Council, and the West Midlands Combined Authority."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Coventry_Cathedral_2018.jpg/330px-Coventry_Cathedral_2018.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coventry"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Coventry_City_Centre_%282020%29_cropped_a_bit.jpg/500px-Coventry_City_Centre_%282020%29_cropped_a_bit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Coventry_City_Centre_%282020%29_cropped_a_bit.jpg/1280px-Coventry_City_Centre_%282020%29_cropped_a_bit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Coventry_City_Centre_%282020%29_cropped_a_bit.jpg/500px-Coventry_City_Centre_%282020%29_cropped_a_bit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACoventry_City_Centre_(2020)_cropped_a_bit.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Whittle_Arch.jpg/500px-Whittle_Arch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Whittle_Arch.jpg/500px-Whittle_Arch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWhittle_Arch.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/The_Council_House%2C_Coventry_%28Cropped%29.jpg/500px-The_Council_House%2C_Coventry_%28Cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/The_Council_House%2C_Coventry_%28Cropped%29.jpg/500px-The_Coun